WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.640
Who are you?

2
00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.340
Shut up! This is a robbery!

3
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.800
Yeah, welcome to the worst apartment for this.

4
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:05.660
Give me the money!

5
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.060
Bro, this morning I checked my account balance

6
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.400
and apologized to the app.

7
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.520
You have nothing?

8
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.340
I have stress, debts and half a jar of sour cream in the fridge.

9
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.420
Where's your jewelry?

10
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:15.600
In photos from 2019.

11
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:16.640
Laptop?

12
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.520
Older than my last relationship.

13
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.540
It works only when you ask it nicely.

14
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:20.320
TV?

15
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.100
Take it if you want, but the remote doesn't work.

16
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.120
You'll have to get up, like in the nineties.

17
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.080
Fine, do you at least have cash?

18
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.480
I have two marks.

19
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:27.820
Only two?

20
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.760
And one coin from Croatia,

21
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.920
but it's no longer valid there either.

22
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:32.700
What do you even do for a living?

23
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.000
Survive. And you?

24
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.300
Looks like the same.

25
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.320
Want some tea?

26
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.940
I came to steal.

27
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.620
I know, but you can see there's nothing to steal.

28
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.820
This is the worst robbery of my career.

29
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.460
And I'm having the worst month of the year, and I'm not whining.

30
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.280
Wait, are you really broke?

31
00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.560
Yes. If you came for money,

32
00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.080
sit down, we'll wait for payday together.

33
00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:51.800
When does it arrive?

34
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.340
God willing, on Friday.

35
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:54.260
And today?

36
00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:55.240
Monday.

37
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.460
Fine, I'm leaving.

38
00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.060
Wait.

39
00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:57.780
What is it?

40
00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.940
Since you're leaving anyway, can you take out the trash?

41
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.240
Are you serious?

42
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.280
Bro, you already walked into my apartment.

43
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.140
At least be useful.